{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And YHWH said: Behold, one people.</b> This statement He said to the angels, and this is the meaning of \"and He came down,\" and its accent is יָרַד, because He said thus." "One people, in that they have one religion, for when religions differ, rivalry and hatred are renewed, and likewise when language differs; therefore the king of Media and Persia commanded: \"and according to the language of his people\" (Esther 1:22)." "And the word הַחִלָם has a patach gadol because of the ḥet that follows it, and likewise הַחֲלֹתִי (Deuteronomy 2:31)." "And the word יִבָּצֵר is like יִמָּנַע, and similar to it: \"fortified cities\" (Deuteronomy 3:5), and this is the meaning: if I leave them, they will suppose that they can do whatever they desire." "And the word יִזַּמּוּ is like זָמָמוּ, and they are two roots:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:10.827040358Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}